From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mm/nommu: fail a private copy larger than the largest block

do_mmap_private() makes a private mapping's copy with alloc_pages_exact(),
which takes one block of the order the length rounds up to.  A length
beyond MAX_PAGE_ORDER cannot be had at all, and the page allocator warns,
with a stack trace, the first time it is asked: any program can do that
with one large mmap() or malloc().  Such a mapping now fails as an
allocation the allocator refused does, with -ENOMEM and the same report.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
---
--- a/mm/nommu.c
+++ b/mm/nommu.c
@@ -967,6 +967,9 @@ static int do_mmap_private(struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 	 *   we're allocating is smaller than a page
 	 */
 	order = get_order(len);
+	/* No block beyond MAX_PAGE_ORDER can hold the copy. */
+	if (order > MAX_PAGE_ORDER)
+		goto enomem;
 	total = 1 << order;
 	point = len >> PAGE_SHIFT;
 
